The below stage in the Jenkinsfile for the Pipeline takes care of the initial setup and installation of Prometheus and Grafana:

stage('Deploy Monitoring Stack') {
            steps {
               withCredentials([[
                   $class: 'AmazonWebServicesCredentialsBinding',
                   credentialsId: "${AWS_CREDENTIALS_ID}"
               ]]) {
                   sh """
                       aws eks update-kubeconfig --region ${AWS_REGION} --name ${EKS_CLUSTER_NAME}

                       helm repo add prometheus-community https://prometheus-community.github.io/helm-charts
                       helm repo update

                       helm upgrade --install kube-prometheus-stack prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack \
                       --namespace devsecops --create-namespace

                       kubectl apply -f k8s/grafana-service.yaml
                  """
               }
           }
       }		






Command to get the admin username password for Grafana:
kubectl --namespace devsecops get secrets kube-prometheus-stack-grafana -o jsonpath="{.data.admin-password}" | base64 -d ; echo

kubectl get all -n devsecops

kubectl get svc -n devsecops
